# Pen of the HP Elite Dragonfly Chromebook (Google Redrix): a single tip, no barrel button, no eraser
# (checked on evdev 2026-10-09: only BTN_TOOL_PEN and BTN_TOUCH ever fire; the controller still
# advertises BTN_TOOL_RUBBER, BTN_STYLUS and BTN_STYLUS2). libwacom's generic styli all declare two
# buttons, so GNOME would offer mappings for buttons that do not exist. The ID sits just below
# libwacom's own generic range (0xffffb-0xfffff) and is local to this machine.
[0x0:0xffff0]
Name=Redrix Pen
Group=redrix-pen
Buttons=0
Axes=Pressure;
Type=General
IsGenericStylus=true
